  ('courmayeur-italy', '02F', 'Courmayeur', 'Italy', 'The Italian side of Mont Blanc', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Italian Alps', '{"ski","adventure","ultra","romance","wellness","culinary"}', '{"alpine","refined","dramatic"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Courmayeur at 1,224 m on the Italian side of Monte Bianco (Mont Blanc), Aosta Valley; spa resort since the 18th c; alpinism from the 19th c","Skyway Monte Bianco (opened 2015, ~EUR 138M — world''s most expensive cable car): Pontal d''Entreves 1,300 m -> Pavillon du Mont-Frety 2,173 m -> Punta Helbronner 3,466 m, rotating 80-person cabins","Ski area Courmayeur-Checrouit/Val Veny: 41.5 km pistes (16 easy/21.5 int/4 diff), 1,205-2,755 m, 18 lifts, ~1,550 m vertical; season ~28 Nov 2026-4 Apr 2027","Toula Glacier + Vallee Blanche off-piste from Punta Helbronner (guided-only); Courmayeur alpine-guide society founded 1850 (2nd in the world)","Pre-Saint-Didier QC Terme thermal baths: 40+ experiences, outdoor pools with Mont Blanc views, entry from ~EUR 46; adults 14+","Skyway return fares 2026: Punta Helbronner adult ~EUR 59-63; Pavillon ~EUR 25-27; SkyVertigo walkway + 360 observatory + ~900-species botanical garden + Torino Hut link","Monte Bianco Ski & Snowboard School (founded 1936, Italy''s largest) turns 90 in 2026; Mont Blanc Tunnel to Chamonix opened 16 Jul 1965","Summer trail calendar: Gran Trail Courmayeur (GTC30/55/100, 10-12 Jul 2026) + UTMB (from 28 Aug 2026, ~174 km, ~9,900 m climb); Courmayeur Design Week + Italia Polo Challenge"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (single EU number — police/fire/ambulance + Soccorso Alpino Valdostano alpine rescue, 24/7)","hospital":"Ospedale Regionale Umberto Parini, Aosta (Viale Ginevra 3, ~35 km), 24/7 pronto soccorso; alpine casualties by helicopter evac","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine Mont Blanc massif: off-piste avalanche risk (Aosta Valley bulletin via Fondazi